    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23741v1</id>
    <title>The Italian lawmaking process: a unified and structured dataset</title>
    <updated>2026-10-16T16:52:11Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23741v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.23741v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>The Italian legislative process is documented in detailed parliamentary records hosted in institutional websites. However, much of this information is available only as unstructured text, limiting its systematic reuse. We applied a controlled, systematic LLM-based extraction procedure, validated against manually annotated records, to convert these texts into ordered and dated events including, e.g., bill introduction, committee examination, plenary examination, and approval. The resulting dataset reconstructs the procedural histories of all 5346 Italian laws enacted between 1985 and 2026, spanning parliamentary terms IX to XIX, for overall 101413 events. Each event records the activity, date, and chamber, with additional procedural details where available. The dataset supports research in the emerging fields of computational legal and legislative studies, potentially combined with process-oriented data science methods to examine procedural paths and legislative timing across parliamentary terms.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
