    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23245v1</id>
    <title>MGE-PO: Entropy-Aware Credit Assignment for Mathematical Reasoning</title>
    <updated>2026-10-16T10:15:02Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23245v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.23245v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>GRPO assigns the same group-relative advantage to equally rewarded responses within a question, leaving their generation uncertainty unused. We introduce MGE-PO, centered on four-quadrant (4Q) advantage shaping that combines verified correctness with rollout generation entropy. Correctness determines the sign of an additional correction, while entropy controls its magnitude: lower-entropy successes receive larger bonuses and higher-entropy failures receive larger penalties. An online entropy-based question curriculum supports this credit rule using cached rollout measurements. At the final checkpoint after eight training epochs on Qwen3-8B-Base, adding 4Q across three policy optimization settings yields absolute gains of 3.23-3.69% in six-benchmark macro avg@32 and 4.24-11.06% in macro pass@32. On Qwen2.5-7B-Base, the complete configuration raises four-benchmark macro avg@32 from 41.5% to 45.4%.</summary>
